[{"id":"VRCE-6-71-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":1,"english":"As Lakşmaņa devoted to his brother was comforting Rāma, Vibhīşaņa, posting his forces at their proper quarters, came there, surrounded by four heroes accoutred in various arms, resembling masses of collyrium or leaders of elephant-herds.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.89,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3f1a0591b4156d363402be52348a2410b84a813f798532d5a38e78881e7f460a","compact":"ebc41d7858bfcc0bbf42f9149448a2343de1403553c516d5f60eeda660d0f025","nasal":"ebc41d7858bfcc0bbf42f9149448a2343de1403553c516d5f60eeda660d0f025"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":2,"english":"As Lakşmaņa devoted to his brother was comforting Rāma, Vibhīşaņa, posting his forces at their proper quarters, came there, surrounded by four heroes accoutred in various arms, resembling masses of collyrium or leaders of elephant-herds.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.597,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f34d7f57e239afc1de474cd4ea235d4f9e2310cd78018103ff3799ed4fe592e6","compact":"df8479ad872868e28f6a40c8d540a834680d70417d2d2927386d7ec865ed4be1","nasal":"f60cfa23eab9b00305271d09e1790e721cbd4b355e288a06bda0325bacb3b695"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":3,"english":"And approaching the high-souled Rāghava, overwhelmed with grief, he saw the monkeys with tears in their eyes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.617,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a09d5f4014daa2c9d91eaa8530f8393afc22a25c384e48d1e360bc2f34b81134","compact":"cda51803a31618e8a07596e0d746b4507ab0c6d63d0ea3b9e0d453aa0f92dca0","nasal":"cda51803a31618e8a07596e0d746b4507ab0c6d63d0ea3b9e0d453aa0f92dca0"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":4,"english":"He saw that joy of the Ikşvāku race the high-souled Raghava-stupefied with grief, lying on the lap of Lakşmaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"313952a8062561a9aff70e69a108f299700a30757ece41c9892eb1021c133bea","compact":"4f43be745b26b87c35d5fda5330ce177298a31e8e5e41a7f9e8b95605b3d2157","nasal":"b40df367b4b692a8b5df1be5536c5aa4a1565fe23bf2f24fb25f0980ecb3b9ef"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":5,"english":"son Seeing Rāma cast down and inflamed with grief, Vibhisana, inlay pained, said, \"What is this?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0b9832f6d2807e63440d4cc09a9148ab5d756c945436a996aaab93b660728a80","compact":"5f33fdb06263be9a610b104d01ee156aa5ce6fabb8ce5f14d4e88519b9c8ea76","nasal":"cad764043bda49cb9ec6115c14f12c54b108f21330c6b4d2e184102b0cd447ef"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":6,"english":"Thereat, gazing at Vibhisana's countenance as well as all those monkeys, Laksmana, with his eyes flooded with tears, said these words pregnant with dire import.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.612,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7319545eef4e817ce75ce64f9e43e66e48bdabe8bc76ac313027e4fbb70feac7","compact":"1d0b47e9aa5b35f6b17090be2381755e06ab551fedeadef40951fee12027da6e","nasal":"1d0b47e9aa5b35f6b17090be2381755e06ab551fedeadef40951fee12027da6e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":7,"english":"O placid one, hearing from Hanumān's lips that Sītā has been slain by Indrajit. Rāghava has been overcome with stupor.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.69,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5740949a89422b74c130e33fef892e0cbb3d9c31da3fd45559c2352d870e33bc","compact":"986ac71368eda8ac33733b1c6b9136213a2076083be6a8ace49f817054aee3f9","nasal":"0baec24759da7e64a427d23cc22de474ce69c32501f48d362cf71afa889a9bd9"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":8,"english":"As Sumitra's was speaking thus, Vibhisana,. preventing him, addressed the stupefied Rāma in these pregnant words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d4935e62ec81fbab4e87b74546eb3d1a452750bd0069e7032eff0562d42d06ee","compact":"970e660870ecc01da8df7071fd9f71a9b7576765e7b648cb27270939bfb860d1","nasal":"b799d5201a01cf6e1c4f5525725e9f4952b428c700a4f8dabe6473ce444fd24f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":9,"english":"O king, all that Hanumān in distressful guise had communicated to you I deem as improbable, like to the drying of the deep.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"865f1cbfd0999918b3f69d264f2a25d92749eba26718c4fa1c0e11d5f64417dd","compact":"e801348af83e2982081da2ecd4180ed6aec741fc9e6f9ee036124d5dc826d03c","nasal":"0655d4b0824f9de0502108b262d5b535f1341d976741b540d3b94eba5c27254b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":10,"english":"I know the intent of the impious Rāvana with reference to Sita, O mighty-armed one. Her he will not slay.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3d2b84e058ac19970a7059930f9854a9460f22dfcc7f1b24d9fb45fe3eba2077","compact":"7861ca749674c18d2772e89500bdde2bf5192fabd5f9e430e216662634c240f3","nasal":"7861ca749674c18d2772e89500bdde2bf5192fabd5f9e430e216662634c240f3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":11,"english":"I, seeking his welfare, had besought him much, saying, 'Let go Vaidehi', but he did not act up to my speech.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a5041b5ee8c837c07c9b7b9953206418ac4a1ae96c74ea8304e8d7b3db35803f","compact":"47671614e519dd64e2482498a83f86a5385e7b66bde5cda57083ad83937a8536","nasal":"47671614e519dd64e2482498a83f86a5385e7b66bde5cda57083ad83937a8536"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":12,"english":"Neither by conciliation, nor by gift, nor by dissension, and where is war? nor by any other means is one capable of obtaining the very sight of Sītā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.719,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"961d2cbc17c0b4be456404cad45174f76e38aa625214c4d8a924b59180613824","compact":"1068194e21d8bd60fd06b394414638f5532a387d1099843221cdf22601235a22","nasal":"1068194e21d8bd60fd06b394414638f5532a387d1099843221cdf22601235a22"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":13,"english":"Having bewildered the monkeys, the Raksasa has gone back; and, O mighty-armed one, know her to be the illusory daughter of Janaka.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.438,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"19376209df79666e6b873dc4142d61668ea7ce82ace3e81aaab537c4c0b5130d","compact":"223a83302fef20a63b5ef8cbb83f6e54af564f03780a059a606dfbd42c26441a","nasal":"a3460c368492ca97ef42eec51ff360f69600b83f36c9c1b50fd4d7004419da51"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":14,"english":"Today, going to the sacrificial ground (called) Nikumbhilā, he will offer oblations into fire; and there the deity of fire will present himself along with Vasava and the (other) divinities. Then Rāvana's son shall be invincible in batile. Indubitably that illusion has been wrought by him, to deceive (the monkeys), so that they might not through their prowess disturb him there.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.491,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-13","DUTT-6-84-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"12e7da489e290d30c1effe507962ed94d8c8af3368ad06ea6244a2cd1873f9f5","compact":"607dfedf76c54004a1dc9f3fe8bf2e49562a54a507f5826ccbb7a6cb9c1a3eaa","nasal":"607dfedf76c54004a1dc9f3fe8bf2e49562a54a507f5826ccbb7a6cb9c1a3eaa"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":15,"english":"Thither will we go before he has furnished his (sacrifice). O foremost of men, shake off this vain sorrow that has overcome you!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.591,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f65da4f99a1b74da7f12eb9a048f346e8c59a947560ab249a643f71ebb1329fe","compact":"6020920add4109c18457d643dbc1cff493e4dce4d33d7852f406f6f77c7dc944","nasal":"dd143a93417563aecd08a01f4aa5b02b53e6d13b616356fd22ef408316a024c5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":16,"english":"Seeing you smitten with grief, this entire host is dispirited. Here, with your heart composed, do your stay, summoning your strength. Send Lakşmañana along with us and the flower of the forces.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.908,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-84-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6071016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b9e2280fe7f49fdded242358a6d8dec36d33e41be26bc9ee5ff786bc829d86b9","compact":"6cbb236d45dbb147d7d078d59658589529ec963ec89eeae9c8b9069579a572e8","nasal":"6cbb236d45dbb147d7d078d59658589529ec963ec89eeae9c8b9069579a572e8"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-71-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":71,"verse":17,"english":"Seeing you smitten with grief, this entire host is dispirited. Here, with your heart composed, do your stay, summoning your strength. Send Lakşmañana along with us and the flower of the forces.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.904,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","du